// Sanora production dart-defines, baked into the iOS Release build.
//
// Why this file exists: Flutter passes --dart-define values to the native
// build through Generated.xcconfig, which is git-ignored and rewritten by
// every `flutter` command. A `flutter run`, a `flutter build ios` without
// --dart-define-from-file, or an Xcode "Product > Archive" therefore produces
// a binary with an EMPTY DART_DEFINES — no SUPABASE_URL, so AppConfig.hasSupabase
// is false and the app boots into offline-only mode. A build like that once
// reached TestFlight and showed "This build has no backend configured".
//
// Included after Generated.xcconfig in Release.xcconfig, this appends the
// production backend to whatever Generated.xcconfig holds. When the build DID
// pass the flag, the values are simply repeated (last wins, same value); when
// it did not, they are the only copy — so a Release build always has a backend.
//
// The values are base64-encoded `KEY=VALUE` pairs, the exact format Flutter
// itself writes. Only SUPABASE_ANON_KEY is a credential, and it is the
// publishable key that already ships in every client binary; row-level security
// is what protects the data, not the secrecy of this key. Do NOT put the
// service-role key or the Gemini key here — those live only in the backend.
//
// This file is Release-only. Debug and Profile builds still come from the
// flutter command line, so `flutter run` against a local or dev backend is
// unaffected.

DART_DEFINES=$(inherited),U1VQQUJBU0VfVVJMPWh0dHBzOi8vZmJzd3NhZnF6eHlwcXppYmFvZ24uc3VwYWJhc2UuY28=,U1VQQUJBU0VfQU5PTl9LRVk9c2JfcHVibGlzaGFibGVfd08tTzZ1ZDFIQ2xLZGNIamRzSk13Z19uNDZvUG45bw==,UkVMRUFTRV9DSEFOTkVMPXByb2R1Y3Rpb24=
